Overdispersion: Poisson Pearson chi2/df = 1.58 (n_unint), 1.16 (n_gard), 2.04 (n_total) -> NB preferred.
NB vs Poisson (n_unint): LR=65.4, p=6.7e-16; NB alpha=1.15 (SE 0.25) -> overdispersion confirmed, NB is the supported count model.
Zero-inflation: ZIP AIC 909.4 < NB AIC 925.0 (n_unint) indicates zero-inflation is present, BUT the ZIP/ZINB fits were
numerically unstable (convergence + Hessian-inversion warnings) and the count-part urban coefficient collapsed to ~0
(the urban signal moved into the zero-ALWAYS-ABSENT component, inflate_intercept p<0.001). => the urban effect operates
through OCCUPANCY/PRESENCE, consistent with the presence-logit; we keep the converged NB as the primary count model
(urban IRR=1.51, p=4.1e-06 at 500 m). n_agfo too sparse (96% zeros, max=2) for stable count estimation; low power.
