FINAL - CANDIDATE HYPOTHESIS (data-grounded)
========================================================================================
HYPOTHESIS: In Barcelona province (Catalonia), URBAN LAND USE promoted the invasion of non-native plants
introduced UNINTENTIONALLY (via global trade and tourism) -- predominantly ruderal ANNUAL forbs -- in the
scenario of URBANIZED LANDSCAPES: plots in the Urban habitat and in surroundings with high current urban cover
(500-1000 m buffers) resulting from urbanization since 1956 (current 2009 cover operative; pre-1956 baseline not).
Unintentional presence OR per +1SD urban_2009: 1.83 [1.48,2.27] (50 m), 2.01 [1.57,2.57] (500 m), 1.92 [1.48,2.49] (1000 m); all p<1e-6.
NB count IRR per +1SD urban_2009 (n_unint): 1.36 (50 m, p=1.5e-5), 1.51 (500 m, p=4.1e-6), 1.38 (1000 m, p=5.9e-4).
HEAD-TO-HEAD TYPE DISCRIMINATION: gardening OR=1.36 [1.08,1.71] (p=0.008, 500 m) - much weaker; agriforest ns (OR 0.89, p=0.67).
Among invaded plots, the unintentional share of occurrences RISES with urban cover (share_unint slope +0.20/unit-z, p=0.006,
1000 m) while the gardening share FALLS (p=0.030) and log(gard/unint) DECREASES (p=0.008).
Urban habitat: mean n_unint=1.60 (presence 75%) vs 0.33 non-urban (17%); total non-natives 2.32 vs 0.58 (fold 3.99).
CONTRAST/CONTEXT: gardening is the dominant recent INTRODUCTION pathway (75% of 1985-2019 introductions, chi2 p=6e-47) but is NOT
the type specifically promoted by urban land cover; agriforest shows no urban association. Unintentional invaders are also the most
successful species regionally (mean invaded plots 9.6, AOO 6.2, habitat range 2.8, invaded niche 0.75; e.g. Erigeron sumatrensis,
Amaranthus retroflexus, Symphyotrichum squamatum, Erigeron canadensis).